1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,217
In Class 1, you wrote a mission with one map in it.

2
00:00:06,117 --> 00:00:10,465
This class is about a mission that's a whole universe,

3
00:00:10,915 --> 00:00:16,567
with many systems, and a game you can stop and pick up again.

4
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:21,846
And this is the first minute of yours:

5
00:00:22,296 --> 00:00:27,513
a title, a place to start with a name you gave it,

6
00:00:27,963 --> 00:00:29,702
and a save file.

7
00:00:30,602 --> 00:00:33,211
It's one file of your own,

8
00:00:33,661 --> 00:00:36,704
and a few words changed in another.

9
00:00:37,904 --> 00:00:40,948
You know this command from Class 1,

10
00:00:41,398 --> 00:00:44,007
and only one word is different.

11
00:00:44,907 --> 00:00:48,385
The template isn't a m d any more,

12
00:00:48,835 --> 00:00:51,443
it's o u, for Open Universe.

13
00:00:52,343 --> 00:00:54,952
So this is a new folder,

14
00:00:55,402 --> 00:00:59,315
and you're not building on your Class 1 mission.

15
00:01:01,115 --> 00:01:05,463
Then I fetch its libraries, the way I did before,

16
00:01:05,913 --> 00:01:07,652
and I run lint.

17
00:01:08,552 --> 00:01:12,900
It says clean, and I haven't written a word yet.

18
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,409
It even plays as it is.

19
00:01:16,859 --> 00:01:21,207
Everything from here is me replacing what I was given.

20
00:01:22,407 --> 00:01:24,146
Three files matter today.

21
00:01:25,046 --> 00:01:28,089
There's the universe itself, which I write.

22
00:01:28,539 --> 00:01:33,757
There's the story file, which tells the game which universe to load.

23
00:01:34,207 --> 00:01:38,989
And there's the one line for the game's list of missions,

24
00:01:39,439 --> 00:01:41,613
which already has my title.

25
00:01:43,413 --> 00:01:46,022
Notice there's no file called mission.

26
00:01:46,922 --> 00:01:52,139
In this kind of mission, the fact sheet is the universe file,

27
00:01:52,589 --> 00:01:55,198
and I get to name it.

28
00:01:56,398 --> 00:02:00,311
So first, I give the file my own name.

29
00:02:01,211 --> 00:02:06,428
Then the record at the top, the one with a single hash.

30
00:02:07,328 --> 00:02:10,807
One hash means, this is the universe itself,

31
00:02:11,257 --> 00:02:15,170
and there's only one of those in the file.

32
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:22,187
Inside the fence is the word Universe, on a line by itself.

33
00:02:22,637 --> 00:02:30,028
It says what kind of record this is, just as the word Arc did in Class 1.

34
00:02:30,928 --> 00:02:34,841
Under the fence I write what this place is.

35
00:02:35,741 --> 00:02:38,350
Now here's the thing to know:

36
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:42,713
the game never shows this record to a player.

37
00:02:43,613 --> 00:02:46,657
It's the title page of my manuscript,

38
00:02:47,107 --> 00:02:50,150
and it's for me and my co-writers.

39
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:55,263
Next comes a chapter, with two hashes, called Scenario.

40
00:02:56,163 --> 00:02:58,772
It holds one line today, Mode,

41
00:02:59,222 --> 00:03:03,570
and the mode says what kind of game this is.

42
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:07,513
Story is one ship and an ending.

43
00:03:07,963 --> 00:03:11,441
Campaign is a long game over many evenings.

44
00:03:11,891 --> 00:03:15,370
Sandbox is an open world with no ending.

45
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:19,343
Today all three play alike,

46
00:03:19,793 --> 00:03:24,141
so I write the one that's true of my story.

47
00:03:25,041 --> 00:03:28,954
And the key has to be the word scenario,

48
00:03:29,404 --> 00:03:32,883
because that's the word the game looks for.

49
00:03:34,083 --> 00:03:36,257
Now the place they start.

50
00:03:37,157 --> 00:03:41,070
At the bottom I add a chapter called Landmarks,

51
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:44,998
and one landmark under it, with three hashes.

52
00:03:45,898 --> 00:03:49,376
The line At says which system it's in,

53
00:03:49,826 --> 00:03:54,174
and zero, zero is home, where every new game begins.

54
00:03:55,974 --> 00:03:58,583
That one record does three things.

55
00:03:59,483 --> 00:04:03,396
When the crew arrives, a card names the system,

56
00:04:03,846 --> 00:04:06,889
and shows my line under the name.

57
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:10,833
There's a station there with that name.

58
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:16,080
And it goes on the crew's list of charted places,

59
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:19,574
so they can find their way back.

60
00:04:21,374 --> 00:04:25,722
Keep the line under the fence to one short line,

61
00:04:26,172 --> 00:04:29,215
because the card only shows the first.

62
00:04:30,115 --> 00:04:35,333
And it cuts anything past sixty characters, so mine is just fifty.

63
00:04:36,533 --> 00:04:40,880
The story file still has the template's names in it.

64
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:43,954
So I press control H,

65
00:04:44,404 --> 00:04:48,317
I search for My Universe, and it finds four.

66
00:04:49,217 --> 00:04:52,261
I replace all four with my title.

67
00:04:53,161 --> 00:04:56,639
Then I search for the old file name,

68
00:04:57,089 --> 00:05:00,133
it finds two, and I replace those.

69
00:05:01,933 --> 00:05:04,976
If your counts aren't four and two,

70
00:05:05,426 --> 00:05:08,035
stop and look before you replace.

71
00:05:09,835 --> 00:05:13,313
Next, the two lines under the map line.

72
00:05:13,763 --> 00:05:18,111
Those are what a player reads on the start screen,

73
00:05:18,561 --> 00:05:20,735
so I write my own.

74
00:05:21,635 --> 00:05:25,983
And these two lines near the top I leave alone.

75
00:05:26,883 --> 00:05:29,926
The first gives Helm an Engage button,

76
00:05:30,376 --> 00:05:34,289
and the second keeps the list of charted places.

77
00:05:35,489 --> 00:05:39,402
Lint reads both files now, and it says clean.

78
00:05:41,202 --> 00:05:45,985
But I want you to see the one it can't catch.

79
00:05:46,885 --> 00:05:52,102
I change a single letter of the title, on this one line,

80
00:05:52,552 --> 00:05:54,726
and lint still says clean.

81
00:05:55,626 --> 00:05:59,104
If I played that, my universe wouldn't load.

82
00:05:59,554 --> 00:06:04,337
The game would start anyway, with a place called Home Port,

83
00:06:04,787 --> 00:06:07,830
and none of my work in it.

84
00:06:08,730 --> 00:06:14,383
So the title has to be spelled the same way, all four times.

85
00:06:15,283 --> 00:06:17,891
If it ever happens to you,

86
00:06:18,341 --> 00:06:22,254
the runtime log in your mission folder says so.

87
00:06:23,154 --> 00:06:25,328
I put the letter back.

88
00:06:26,528 --> 00:06:31,746
Here's the card, with my station's name on it, and my line.

89
00:06:32,646 --> 00:06:35,254
On Comms, I select a station,

90
00:06:35,704 --> 00:06:39,183
and I take the cargo run it offers.

91
00:06:40,083 --> 00:06:43,561
Then on Helm, I open the Quest Log,

92
00:06:44,011 --> 00:06:47,489
I pick the run, and I press Engage.

93
00:06:48,389 --> 00:06:50,998
And that's the jump you're watching.

94
00:06:52,798 --> 00:06:56,276
We're somewhere new, and the run has paid.

95
00:06:57,176 --> 00:07:00,220
And look at this group, Charted Locations.

96
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,843
Kestrel Relay is in it,

97
00:07:03,293 --> 00:07:05,467
and that's my way home.

98
00:07:06,367 --> 00:07:08,976
But I'm not going home yet.

99
00:07:09,426 --> 00:07:12,035
I'm closing the game right here.

100
00:07:13,235 --> 00:07:15,843
This is what the game kept.

101
00:07:16,743 --> 00:07:19,787
It's a file named after my title,

102
00:07:20,237 --> 00:07:23,280
and here's the system I stopped in.

103
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:28,993
I start the game again, with the same command,

104
00:07:29,443 --> 00:07:34,661
and I'm where I left off, with the money from the run.

105
00:07:35,561 --> 00:07:40,343
Then I pick Kestrel Relay, I press Engage, and we're home.

106
00:07:42,143 --> 00:07:45,187
Two things to remember about that file.

107
00:07:46,087 --> 00:07:48,261
It's named from the title,

108
00:07:48,711 --> 00:07:53,928
so if you change the title, you start a new, empty game.

109
00:07:54,828 --> 00:07:57,437
And to begin again on purpose,

110
00:07:57,887 --> 00:08:00,930
close the game and delete the file.

111
00:08:02,130 --> 00:08:03,870
Now make it yours:

112
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:09,537
your title, your file name, your home port, and your two lines.

113
00:08:10,437 --> 00:08:16,524
Before you play, write down what you think the save file will be called,

114
00:08:16,974 --> 00:08:19,148
and then go and look.

115
00:08:20,948 --> 00:08:24,426
Next time, we fill this place with people:

116
00:08:24,876 --> 00:08:28,354
three factions, and one of them shoots first.
